## 1. Executive Summary & Forensic Audit Resolution

Under the 24 September 2026 human authorization, an exhaustive line-by-line forensic audit, spatial sensitivity study, literature-faithful coarse continuum pre-analysis, triangular element subroutine verification, native Abaqus adaptive mesh generation, and complete production solve execution for the Pandey & Kumar (2025) Mode-II benchmark was executed.

### 1.1 Conclusive Resolution of the Stiffness Discrepancy ($2906\text{ kN/mm}$ vs $12.8\text{ kN/mm}$)

The earlier apparent stiffness discrepancy between the staged Gen-3 diagnostic run response ($K_0 \approx 2906.15\text{ kN/mm}$) and the literature-faithful Mode-II baseline ($K_0 \approx 12.83\text{ kN/mm}$) was **conclusively and uniquely resolved to a single implementation defect**: an **input-deck UEL Property ABI indexing mismatch**.

The speculative second root cause—suggesting that $K_0 \approx 12.8\text{ kN/mm}$ was flexure-dominated and that pure shear required $K_0 \approx 45-75\text{ kN/mm}$—is **fully retracted**. Detailed boundary condition and kinematic analysis confirms that for the standard Pandey & Kumar (2025) Section 4.2 literature-faithful candidate ($1\times 1\text{ mm}$ domain, bottom clamped $u_x=u_y=0$, horizontal displacement $u_x$ applied along the top edge, top $u_y$ left free), the project-derived initial linear elastic stiffness is **$K_0 \approx 12.83\text{ kN/mm}$**.

